/Title (The object-oriented paradigm in OOAD organizes a system around objects instead of functions or procedures, where each object encapsulates both data and behaviors representing real-world entities. Its goal is to model software in a way that reflects real-world structures and interactions. This approach enhances clarity, reusability, and maintainability of the system.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 643 0 R
/Prev 790 0 R
/First 857 0 R
/Last 857 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
